 m_bUseCVON 1
 m_aMissionDescriptors {
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1A503377C}" {
   m_sTitle "Mission: Situation"
   m_sTextData "Kolguyev, east coast, 0700. Overcast, calm sea."\
   ""\
   "The beach between Gorshkovo and the naval harbour is the only stretch of open shore on this coast. A US Marine platoon holds it from the old coastal defences: a concrete sea wall along the top of the sand, hedgehogs and dragon's teeth on the beach, Tobruk MG pits, two casemates and hill bunkers above them, and MG nests covering the south draw and the harbour road. Behind the beach the ground climbs past the mining village of Gorshkovo and its coal silo to the Nadezhda coal mine on the ridge, 1.2 km inland and 200 m up."\
   ""\
   "A Russian motor-rifle company is launching its BTR-70s from a pontoon 850 m offshore."\
   ""\
   "OPFOR: Russian motor-rifle company (-) in eight BTR-70s: HQ, six rifle squads (1-1 to 1-3, 2-1 to 2-3), a sapper squad (SAPPER) and an 82 mm mortar crew (MORTAR)."\
   "BLUFOR: US Marine rifle platoon (CP, SQUAD 1-3) with a machine-gun section of three M240 teams (GUNS). Dug in, no vehicles."
   m_aFactionKeys {
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1F61769E7}" {
   m_sTitle "OPFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Three objectives, one after another (the task list shows the open one and its progress):"\
   "1. Breach the sea wall and control Red Beach."\
   "2. Capture the observation post at the coal silo."\
   "3. Capture the command post (Nadezhda mine)."\
   ""\
   "1. RED BEACH"\
   "A concrete sea wall runs along the top of the sand, too high to climb and too solid to ram. Six sections of it are breach points (marked on your map): a sapper with a satchel charge or a TNT block uses \"Place breaching charge\" on the seaward side of one. The charge is used up and the section blows 10 seconds later - get clear. One breach is enough; a blown section leaves a 4 m gap. Then hold Red Beach (the beach and the slope up to the casemates): at least 3 of you, at most 2 Marines, for 60 seconds."\
   "2. COAL SILO"\
   "The Marines' observation post is the tower and the camouflaged post on the silo pad above Gorshkovo. At least 2 of you, at most 1 Marine, for 45 seconds."\
   "3. NADEZHDA MINE"\
   "The Marine command post is in the mine yard on the ridge, 1.2 km inland and 200 m up: three huts, tents and the flag. At least 3 of you, at most 1 Marine, for 90 seconds."\
   "If nobody is there to hold a zone, its progress drains; contested, it holds."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "Each element spawns on the pontoon next to its own BTR-70, which floats alongside the dock: board it from the deck. A rifle squad fills one BTR - driver, gunner and seven in the back. The squad's driver and gunner stay with the vehicle and support with its 14.5 mm KPVT and PKT. HQ and SAPPER share the seventh BTR, MORTAR has the eighth."\
   "The BTRs swim. The run in is slow, about five minutes, and every M240 and AT4 on the bluff is waiting for you. Hedgehogs and dragon's teeth cover the sand, and the sea wall stops the vehicles until it is breached: get the sappers to the wall, keep the BTRs' guns on the bunkers."\
   ""\
   "SAPPERS: four combat engineers, each with three satchel charges, a 400 g TNT block and a blasting machine - every one of them can blow a breach point."\
   "MORTAR: an 82 mm 2B14 crew. The gunner and the loader carry the tube, bipod and base plate and ten rounds (5 HE, 5 smoke); the crew chief has the firing table. Set up once you are ashore."\
   ""\
   "No timed respawns: when an objective falls, everyone dead comes back - after the beach at the beachhead behind the wall, after the silo on the road below it. A destroyed BTR is replaced at the pontoon when an objective falls."\
   ""\
   "CASUALTIES: the company can take two and a half times as many casualties as it has men when safe start ends. Every death counts, again after a respawn. Reach that and the Marines win (the pause menu shows the count)."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E199D38E4F}" {
   m_sTitle "BLUFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Hold three positions, one after another: the sea wall and Red Beach, the observation post at the coal silo, the command post at the Nadezhda mine."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "You start on the slope above the beach. Beach Red is fortified with the old coastal defences: the sea wall along the top of the sand, sandbag bunkers on the beach, Tobruk MG pits, two casemates (ladder to the roof) and hill bunkers above them, MG nests at the south draw and on the harbour road."\
   "The Russians come in eight BTR-70s that swim in from a pontoon 850 m out; the crossing takes them about five minutes. Each BTR has a 14.5 mm KPVT that outranges your M240s and goes through sandbags: fight from the concrete, and save the AT4s for a BTR that is close. The sea wall, the hedgehogs and the dragon's teeth keep the vehicles on the sand until the wall is breached."\
   "The Russians have to blow a gap in the wall first: you are warned when a breaching charge is set (10 s). After that they take the beach if they hold it for 60 seconds with 2 or fewer of you on it."\
   "When a position falls, everyone dead comes back at the next one: the hill west of Gorshkovo for the silo, the road behind the mine for the command post."\
   "GUNS has three M240 teams, a gunner and an assistant each. Every rifle squad has an M249, a grenadier and two AT4s. Your only corpsman is with the CP."\
   ""\
   "YOU WIN if the Russians have not taken all three when the time limit (60 minutes) runs out, if they are wiped out, or if they reach their casualty limit (two and a half times the men they had when safe start ended; every death counts, again after a respawn; the pause menu shows the count)."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E10A6C267B}" {
   m_sTitle "Administration"
   m_sTextData "Objective chain, 3 objectives. Time limit 75 minutes after safe start (safe start max. 15 minutes)."\
   ""\
   "No timed respawns. When an objective falls, every dead player of both sides respawns at their side's new spawn. Each spawn also updates after each objective."\
   ""\
   "Casualty limit: OPFOR, 250% of its players when safe start ends. This means there can be three respawn waves (300%), but if the 3rd respawn wave receives over 50% casualties, it's a mission fail for OPFOR."\
   ""\
   "Mission by tanaKa-."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6AD978D01806B5C4}" {
   m_sTitle "Administration"
   m_sTextData "N/A"
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
    "OPFOR"
    "INDFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
 }
